  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: scvi_n200/multiprofile/transformer at 0.653), while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208). The largest unexplored design axis is whether multimodal fusion can complement the strong RNA signal with any useful image information. This experiment (config_032) pairs the best RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation) with resnet50 image features via simple concat fusion, isolating the effect of adding the image modality to the already-optimal RNA pipeline. Using resnet50 (rather than untested ViT-L) keeps the image encoder fixed to a known quantity, so any performance change can be attributed to fusion rather than encoder quality. If concat fusion improves on 0.653, the final experiment can test weighted fusion or a stronger image encoder; if it degrades, we confirm that the weak image signal is not complementary and the RNA-only result stands as the best within budget."
}

